  "question": {
    "text": "A coin is biased so that a head is twice as likely to occur as a tail. If the coin is tossed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> times, then the probability of getting two tails and one head is-"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>H</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>T</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>We know that, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>H</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>T</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>T</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>T</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>T</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>H</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>tails and</mtext><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>head</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mtext>for arrangements</mtext></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>tails and</mtext><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>head</mtext></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
